  "worked_solution": "To subtract two mixed numbers, we subtract whole numbers from whole numbers and fractions from fractions. \n\nSubtracting the whole numbers, we get $6-1=5.$\n\nNow we subtract the fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTo subtract the fractions, we need to find the least common multiple of the denominators ($8$ and $6$).\n\n- Multiples of 8: $\\,8,16,24,…$\n\n- Multiples of 6: $\\,6,12,18,24,…$\n\nTherefore, the least common denominator of $8$ and $6$ is $24.$\n\n- To put $\\frac{7}{8}$ over a denominator of $24,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{7\\times 3}{8\\times 3}=\\frac{21}{24}\n$$\n\n- To put $\\frac{5}{6}$ over a denominator of $24,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{5\\times 4}{6\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{24}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{21}{24}-\\frac{20}{24}=\\frac{1}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n6\\,\\frac{7}{8}-1\\,\\frac{5}{6}=5\\,\\frac{1}{24}\n$$",
